{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Speak to Aaron, saying: Any man of your seed.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: here it does not say 'Speak to Aaron and to his sons, saying,' as it says in all the other sections — and the reason is that there He commands in the law of the offerings: 'this is the law of the burnt-offering,' 'this is the law of the meal-offering,' and the sin-offering and the guilt-offering and the like. But if it said here 'Speak to Aaron and to his sons,' it would be fitting to say 'any man of you, throughout your generations,' and He would not intend to warn Aaron himself concerning the law of blemishes, for Aaron is holy to HaShem, entirely whole, and no blemish would be in him; rather, He warns him concerning his seed, that he may warn them throughout their generations. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, explained the many blemishes that disqualify. First He mentioned the blemish of missing limbs — blind or lame; afterward, in smallness, such as the flat-nosed (חרום); and in largeness, such as the elongated (שרוע); afterward, in the breaking of bones — even though all his limbs are present, once the bone is broken he is disqualified; afterward He disqualified even in ugliness of form, such as the hunchback (גבן), and one whose eyes are diseased (הגרעינין); afterward, in the flesh of the body, which must be clean and smooth; afterward He added one in whom there is an abnormal growth, whose testicles are swollen. And it says 'that has a blemish in him' (אשר בו מום), and then repeats 'a blemish in him' (מום בו) — for whether the blemish was born with him or the blemish befell him after he was born, he is disqualified for service. And He then returned and mentioned the blemishes of the animal, for by them they are disqualified for the offering, and He disqualifies in animals even blemishes of formation (מומי היצירה) — and needless to say blemishes of occurrence (מומי המקרה). Blemishes of formation: שרוע וקלוט (elongated and with closed membrane), for they are blemishes from the womb. Blemishes of occurrence: they are עורת (blindness), or broken, or חרוץ (slit), or יבלת (wart), or גרב (mange), or ילפת (eruption); and עורת is one in whom there is a film (עורון) that covered his eye."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:42.040848792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}